From 040c114d80414c3d8aa7a2dcbf7c24630099bd6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:50:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(post): refuse Tormach lathe G76 when the start point
 is above material

The LinuxCNC G76 (no entry taper) moves the insert to each pass's cut
depth at rapid at the start Z. The Tormach lathe post did not read the
record's StartInAir value (PR #2892), so it posted a G76 that starts
inside the bar. g76Why now refuses the cycle by name when StartInAir is
not true, before any block of the cycle is written. A record without
the value (an older cache) is refused until it is regenerated.

The test support keeps the solid bar (G33 goldens, refusal pins) and
adds g76_world: the bar ends at its free end face and the cycle starts
one lead out, at Z16, in free air. The goldens follow in a later commit.

Refs #2878
Fixes #2952

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
